From 0dfeb3a83334cc312f515e37ac9acdc7f4e952d9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 20:28:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 07/15] Cocoa: fix pixel byte order flag, function keys sent as
 text, menu fallback

- CocoImage.mm: RGBA is { a, r, g, b } in memory on any Mac, which is
  alpha-first big-endian for CoreGraphics regardless of the CPU.
  kCGBitmapByteOrder32Host only happened to be right on PowerPC and
  swaps channels on Intel. Use kCGBitmapByteOrder32Big, and
  CGBitmapContextCreate unconditionally (it is the same thing as
  CGBitmapContextCreateWithData without a release callback).
- CocoProc.mm: the manual key dispatch in keyDown: runs whenever
  insertText: was not called, which is the case for every non-text key.
  Arrows, Home/End, F-keys, forward delete etc. have 'characters' in
  0xF700..0xF8FF, so they were dispatched as characters and inserted
  into edit widgets. Skip keys with the function flag or in that range.
- MacMenu.mm: before the item tracked for the menuDidClose: fallback is
  used, check that it still belongs to a live CocoMenuBar; do not fire
  when the menu was closed by Esc; clear target/action of the item
  before invoking it, so that the command cannot run twice if the
  action gets delivered by AppKit as well. Drop unused
  menuItemWasClicked. Remove menu items through a helper that does not
  depend on -removeAllItems (10.6).
- CocoApp.mm: remove the session-wide CGEventTap. Its only effect was
  calling SyncPopupFocus, which acts only on popups with IsCocoActive(),
  and Ctrl::PopUp never creates such. Guard the event monitors with
  __BLOCKS__ rather than __clang__.
- CocoWin.mm: remove NSLog calls from SwizzleNSWindowMethods.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
